  "question": "Evaluate $\\sin[2\\tan^{-1}x]$ for $x>0$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Let $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}x$, so $\\tan\\theta=x$.<br /><br />We know $\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$.<br /><br />Here $\\sin\\theta=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}$ and $\\cos\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}$.<br /><br />Thus $\\sin2\\theta=\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}$.",
